# request: "For the orders service README, annotate our POST /orders handler in
#  routes/orders.ts so a new engineer sees what the key lines do: the body is
#  validated first, so a bad field is a 400 before any write; the Idempotency-Key
#  header means a retried request gets the first reply; the order is one INSERT and
#  starts as pending; and billing and email react to the order.created event."
type: code-annotated
reader: new engineers reading the orders service README
width: 800
direction: down   # the card on top, the callouts under it, two a row
focus: none
out: the OrderSchema fields, error middleware, the cache TTL policy
nodes:
  handler: routes/orders.ts
  handler.src: * {code}   # routes/orders.ts:14-24, verbatim
  notes.n1: 1. Validates the body: a bad\nfield is a 400, before any write
  notes.n2: 2. The client's retry key:\na repeat gets the first reply
  notes.n3: 3. One INSERT; the order\nstarts as pending
  notes.n4: 4. Billing and email react\nto order.created
edges:
